Design a Knowledge Base with Notion-Style Tools
Objectives
Deploy and configure an open-source wiki platform (BookStack) as a self-hosted knowledge base
Architect an information taxonomy applying content classification best practices
Implement cross-referenced documentation with tagging, glossary, and reusable content blocks
Evaluate knowledge base usability through structured heuristic testing
Prerequisites
Comfortable with Linux CLI, Docker, systemd services, and reverse proxy concepts
Understanding of information architecture principles (taxonomy vs. tagging, content hierarchy)
Familiarity with MySQL/MariaDB basics
Basic knowledge of Markdown and WYSIWYG editors
Environment Setup
Al Nafi-provisioned single Linux VM (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS recommended)
Requires Docker Engine and Docker Compose installed
Minimum 2GB RAM, 10GB free disk space
Root or sudo access
Verify environment:

docker --version && docker compose version
sudo systemctl status docker
If Docker is not installed, install it using the official convenience script and enable the service before proceeding.

Task 1: Deploy BookStack via Docker Compose
Requirements:

Deploy BookStack with a MariaDB backend using Docker Compose (no cloud dependencies)
Persist data using named volumes (survive container restarts)
Expose the app on a local port and confirm accessibility via browser or curl
Architecture to implement:

[BookStack App Container] <--> [MariaDB Container]
         |
    Named Volumes (uploads, db-data)
         |
    Host Port 6875 -> Container Port 80
